  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.520 acc) outperforms pca_n2000 (0.485 acc) in singleprofile RNA, establishing scvi_n200 as the stronger RNA encoder. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208 acc). Uncertainty: We have no multiprofile results yet, and this is a critical design axis that affects all downstream multimodal and aggregation choices. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares against config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile) by changing only the profile setting and adding a simple avgpool aggregation, cleanly isolating the multiprofile effect. It uses the best RNA encoder identified so far and the simplest aggregation (avgpool) to avoid confounding with a complex transformer. If multiprofile helps, it justifies investing further in transformer aggregation and multimodal multiprofile configs; if it doesn't, we can prune a large portion of the search space and focus on singleprofile or encoder improvements. This is the highest-information experiment given the current evidence."
}

